@TheOutdoorProgrammer Hi, I have been watching this PR, but it seems stale. So I checked around the code base of OpenCode if there is another feature that could reduce the amount of active tokens in combination with multiple MCPs.

I found that activating `OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_CODE_MODE` works great for me. 

See https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/tree/dev/packages/codemode for the documentation of that feature.

@neriousy It was a decision made by David months ago, all the built-in themes point to that url, I am also not sure if people can make custom themes outside the opencode repo. If they can, would be nice to have this hosted.

But its your pick, anyone works, just want to be sure of how its meant to be used, so I decided to go with what was commited months ago.

Yeah im seeing commits from 8 months ago, with this set, so I think they had a plan or smth idk, then again could be agents just following stuff.
